.TH "EPX\-VENDOR\-LOCATIONS" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-vendor\-locations \- read and change the locations of vendors
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx vendor\-locations [flags]
epx vendor\-locations [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads and changes the locations of vendors, contact emails included. A vendor names its locations in locations, each as \fB{"id": ...}\fR. create and update ID (an upsert) send the JSON body of \fB\-\-file\fR; delete ID sends none.
.PP
Its reads require the vendor.vendor_read scope. Its writes require the vendor.vendor_manage scope.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx vendor\-locations create"
Create one vendor location.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx vendor\-locations create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates the vendor location that the JSON body of \fB\-\-file\fR describes, shaped as \fBepx vendor\-locations get ID \-o json\fR prints one: type (required: HEADQUARTER, WAREHOUSE or OFFICE), contactDetails (required: emails, phones, addressLine1, addressLine2, city, state, postcode, countryCode and tags) and name; leave out \fB"phones"\fR: [] (an empty list), which Emporix refuses (exit 1). Without an id, Emporix makes one, and answers with it; an id that exists already is a conflict (exit 5).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the vendor.vendor_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx vendor\-locations delete"
Delete one vendor location.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx vendor\-locations delete ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the vendor location ID; it sends no body. ID is the ID that \fBepx vendor\-locations list\fR shows; an unknown one is not found. A vendor that names it in locations no longer does.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type ID at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the vendor.vendor_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx vendor\-locations get"
Show one vendor location.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx vendor\-locations get ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the locations of vendors, contact emails included. TYPE is HEADQUARTER, WAREHOUSE or OFFICE, ADDRESS the first address line and TAGS the location\(aqs labels; phone numbers and the rest of the address are only in \fB\-o json\fR.
.PP
Requires the vendor.vendor_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, NAME, TYPE, ADDRESS, POSTCODE, CITY, COUNTRY, EMAILS, TAGS.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx vendor\-locations list"
List vendor locations.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx vendor\-locations list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the locations of vendors, contact emails included. TYPE is HEADQUARTER, WAREHOUSE or OFFICE, ADDRESS the first address line and TAGS the location\(aqs labels; phone numbers and the rest of the address are only in \fB\-o json\fR.
.PP
Requires the vendor.vendor_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, NAME, TYPE, ADDRESS, POSTCODE, CITY, COUNTRY, EMAILS, TAGS.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, passed as given, e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx vendor\-locations update"
Upsert one vendor location.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx vendor\-locations update ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the vendor location ID with the JSON body of \fB\-\-file\fR, shaped as create takes it but without an id, or creates it with that id where none exists (an upsert); it requires type and contactDetails. With metadata.version as \fBepx vendor\-locations get ID \-o json\fR prints it, Emporix replaces it only if nobody changed it since, and answers 409 Conflict (exit 5) otherwise; without metadata.version, it replaces it whatever its version. ID is the ID that \fBepx vendor\-locations list\fR shows.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the vendor.vendor_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
